      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T14:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about this more: If we make this a `Rust::Slice\u003cfontations_ffi::ColorStop\u003e` we would still need a copying conversion, or, again, an unsafe cast on the Rust side.\n\nThe source of the slice is a `skrifa::color::ColorStop` but on the FFI interface we can only use types that are defined in the CXX `ffi` module of the `ffi.rs` source file. But Rust won\u0027t allow us to case from `skrifa::color::ColorStop` to `fontations_ffi::ColorStop` without unsafe. So this suggestion unfortunately would not remove the requirement for `unsafe` blocks.",
      "parentUuid": "a86c3ecd_5083ee4d",
      "revId": "eb0f3c1c303025ecd436eaa20de544074ed1a9de",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
